{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>From a thread to a sandal strap.</b> Every instance of אִם in Scripture, when not followed by a verb, functions as a condition and stands in place of the word שֶׁלֹּא (\"that not\"). Thus he says: <b>I have raised</b> my hand — that not from a thread to a sandal strap will I take anything from you, and <b>that I will not take</b> from all that is yours. So too: \"אִם יִרְאוּ אֶת הָאָרֶץ\" (Numbers 14:23) — that they shall not see. \"אִם אַתֶּם תָּבֹאוּ\" (Numbers 14:30) — that you shall not come. \"חַי ה׳ אִם יוּמַת\" (1 Samuel 15:6) — that he shall not be put to death. \"חַי ה׳ אֲשֶׁר עָמַדְתִּי לְפָנָיו אִם אֶקַּח\" (2 Kings 5:16) — that I shall not take. And many others besides these."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:30:09.901418571Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}